message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Three-Node Graph Routing Simulation: conserved-message ledger with an optional shortcut edge"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/conserved-message-graph-demo"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  A small, dependency-free Python discrete-event simulation that compares a
  three-node message-routing graph with and without an optional bidirectional
  M1-M3 shortcut, under a matched capacity and loss budget. Each directed edge
  has its own capacity, latency and deterministic loss quota. Every tick
  asserts the conserved-message ledger (change in inventory = injections -
  absorptions - losses). The tool reports delivery by deadline, conditional
  latency, undelivered messages, backlog and losses, and includes a stress
  sweep across offered rates. Scope: a graph-routing analogy only. The 'white-
  hole-like', 'black-hole-like' and 'wormhole-like' labels refer to injection,
  absorption and the optional edge; the code does not model general
  relativity, spacetime, physical membranes or any OES32 feature. All results
  are SYNTHETIC.
keywords:
  - research software
  - discrete-event simulation
  - graph routing
  - conservation ledger
  - synthetic data
  - Python
  - New Brunswick
